Phase 0 — Verify your base

Panda MoveIt RViz demo still opens (fake controllers).

RRBot Gazebo still opens and moves (real ros2_control).

✔️ Pass if both still work.

Phase 1 — Make a clean integration package

    Create a new package (e.g., panda_gz_moveit) to hold:

    a Panda URDF/Xacro wrapper,

    controller config (YAML),

    launch for Gazebo + controllers,

    launch for MoveIt + RViz.

    ✔️ Pass if it builds and shows up in ros2 pkg list.

Phase 2 — Prepare Panda for Gazebo (ros2_control)

    In your Panda URDF wrapper:

    Include the Panda model from moveit_resources_panda_description.

    Add ros2_control: hardware = gazebo_ros2_control GazeboSystem.

    Declare transmissions for:

    7 arm joints: panda_joint1 … panda_joint7

    (optional) 2 finger joints: panda_finger_joint1, panda_finger_joint2

    ✔️ Pass if your URDF expands without errors.

Phase 3 — Define controllers

Controller set you will load at runtime:

joint_state_broadcaster

joint_trajectory_controller for the 7 arm joints

(optional) joint_trajectory_controller for the gripper fingers

Ensure the joint lists exactly match Panda joint names.

✔️ Pass if the controller config references the correct joints.

Phase 4 — Gazebo bring-up

Launch Gazebo, publish robot_description, spawn Panda, start ros2_control_node, then load + activate:

joint_state_broadcaster

panda_arm_controller

(optional) panda_gripper_controller

Checkpoints

Robot is visible in Gazebo.

ros2 control list_controllers shows your controllers active.

ros2 control list_hardware_interfaces lists position command/state interfaces for Panda joints.

✔️ Pass if all three checks succeed.

Phase 5 — Switch MoveIt to real controllers

Start MoveIt against the same Panda URDF you spawned in Gazebo.

In MoveIt config:

Disable fake controllers.

Enable ros2_control integration (MoveIt’s simple controller manager).

Map the MoveIt group panda_arm → your arm joint_trajectory_controller.

(Optional) Map hand → your gripper controller.

Start move_group and RViz (MotionPlanning plugin).

✔️ Pass if RViz shows “Connected” and the Planning Scene matches Gazebo pose.

Phase 6 — Plan & Execute (MoveIt → Gazebo)

In RViz MotionPlanning:

Set a joint-space goal (e.g., slightly different joint 2 & 4).

Click Plan then Execute.

Expectations

Trajectory appears in RViz.

Gazebo robot moves and settles at goal.

No controller errors in terminal.

✔️ Pass if trajectory executes in Gazebo smoothly.

(Optional) Repeat with a small Cartesian motion in RViz to confirm end-to-end planning and execution.

Phase 7 — CLI/Script sanity (optional)

As a secondary check (outside RViz), send a tiny JointTrajectory to the arm controller and confirm Gazebo motion.

✔️ Pass if arm moves and joint_states update consistently.